{
  "version": 1,
  "$id": "https://fuaran.dev/wire-format/v1/validate/manifest.json",
  "description": "The Fuaran pre-emit VALIDATE conformance family (WIRE_FORMAT.md 27.8.2). Each vector is a document (`tree`, canonical wire bytes) and the pre-emit defects it carries (`expected`): each defect's `code` and `severity` from validator/defect-vocabulary.json, the `node` id it is raised on (null where the defect names none), and `path`, the JSONPath of that node's object in the tree in the section 29.3 grammar: the occurrence that raised it, a finding judged across the whole tree included (null only where no node of the document raised it). A finding whose subject is a repetition is reported once at each occurrence after the first, located at that occurrence. The expected defects are listed in document order. A host that implements the pre-emit tier validates each tree and asserts that its findings, restricted to the codes its validator-coverage.json declares implemented, are exactly the expected defects restricted to the same codes, each on the stated node; a host whose finding carries a path asserts that the path is the stated one or extends it at a segment boundary. Generated from the reference host's own validator, through its decoder.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "validate-clean-nested",
      "description": "The control: nested Boxes holding Markdown report no defect, so a host that raises anything here disagrees.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"intro\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Intro\"}},{\"id\":\"inner\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"body\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Body\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-switch-empty-statekey-at-index-1",
      "description": "A Switch with an empty stateKey (FUARAN083) as the second child of a Box. The node's path is $.kind.children[1]: an array index is spelled [i] in a finding's location, as in a decode path (sections 6 and 29.3).",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"intro\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Intro\"}},{\"id\":\"sw\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"sw-a\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"A\"}},\"match\":\"a\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"sw-d\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"D\"}},\"stateKey\":\"\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN083",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "sw",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-switch-empty-statekey-at-index-10",
      "description": "The same defect on the eleventh child, so the index has two digits: $.kind.children[10]. A host that orders or compares paths as strings, or spells the index as a dotted segment, disagrees here.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"m0\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"0\"}},{\"id\":\"m1\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"1\"}},{\"id\":\"m2\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"2\"}},{\"id\":\"m3\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"3\"}},{\"id\":\"m4\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"4\"}},{\"id\":\"m5\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"5\"}},{\"id\":\"m6\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"6\"}},{\"id\":\"m7\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"7\"}},{\"id\":\"m8\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"8\"}},{\"id\":\"m9\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"9\"}},{\"id\":\"sw\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"sw-a\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"A\"}},\"match\":\"a\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"sw-d\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"D\"}},\"stateKey\":\"\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN083",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "sw",
          "path": "$.kind.children[10]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-switch-duplicate-match-in-a-case-arm",
      "description": "A Switch whose two cases match the same value (FUARAN082), held in the first case arm of an outer Switch. The node's path is $.kind.cases[0].child: an arm of an ordered list of records carries its index too. Neither state key has a writer in the tree, so the reference also warns FUARAN103 on both Switches, the outer one at the root path $.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"outer\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"inner\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"inner-a\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"A\"}},\"match\":\"x\"},{\"child\":{\"id\":\"inner-b\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"B\"}},\"match\":\"x\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"inner-d\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"D\"}},\"stateKey\":\"inner\"}},\"match\":\"one\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"outer-d\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"D\"}},\"stateKey\":\"outer\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN103",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "outer",
          "path": "$"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN082",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "inner",
          "path": "$.kind.cases[0].child"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN103",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "inner",
          "path": "$.kind.cases[0].child"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-across-default-and-child",
      "description": "One id held by a Box's child and by a Switch's default arm (FUARAN-DUP-ID). The defect is located at the id's SECOND node in document order, $.kind.children[1].kind.default: the node to change is the later one. The Switch's state key has no writer, so the reference also warns FUARAN103 on it.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"First\"}},{\"id\":\"sw\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"sw-a\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"A\"}},\"match\":\"a\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Second\"}},\"stateKey\":\"view\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN103",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "sw",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1]"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "twice",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1].kind.default"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-three-times",
      "description": "One id held by three nodes, the third one level down (FUARAN-DUP-ID). Three occurrences are TWO findings, one at each occurrence after the first, in document order: $.kind.children[1] and $.kind.children[2].kind.children[0]. The count of findings is the count of nodes to change.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"thrice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"One\"}},{\"id\":\"thrice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Two\"}},{\"id\":\"inner\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"thrice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Three\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "thrice",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1]"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "thrice",
          "path": "$.kind.children[2].kind.children[0]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-in-a-list-of-twelve",
      "description": "One id held by the third and the eleventh of twelve children (FUARAN-DUP-ID). Document order puts children[2] before children[10], so the one finding is at $.kind.children[10]. A host that walks or orders positions as strings meets children[10] first and reports children[2].",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"m0\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"0\"}},{\"id\":\"m1\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"1\"}},{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"2\"}},{\"id\":\"m3\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"3\"}},{\"id\":\"m4\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"4\"}},{\"id\":\"m5\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"5\"}},{\"id\":\"m6\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"6\"}},{\"id\":\"m7\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"7\"}},{\"id\":\"m8\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"8\"}},{\"id\":\"m9\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"9\"}},{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"10\"}},{\"id\":\"m11\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"11\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "twice",
          "path": "$.kind.children[10]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-in-the-node-envelope",
      "description": "One id held by the root's envelope fallback and by its child (FUARAN-DUP-ID). The fallback is walked (section 8.1), and the canonical document lists it before the kind (member order), so the fallback is the first occurrence and the finding is at $.kind.children[0]. A host that walks the kind before the envelope reports $.fallback.",
      "tree": "{\"fallback\":{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Fallback\"}},\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"twice\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"Child\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "twice",
          "path": "$.kind.children[0]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-in-the-state-alternatives",
      "description": "One id held by the root's child and by both of the root's state alternatives (FUARAN-DUP-ID). A state alternative is a member of the node object, so it is part of the document (section 8.1): three occurrences are two findings, at $.state.onEmpty and $.state.onLoading. A host that does not walk the state alternatives reports none.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"},\"state\":{\"onEmpty\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},\"onLoading\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}}}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "X",
          "path": "$.state.onEmpty"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "X",
          "path": "$.state.onLoading"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-in-the-envelope-kind-and-state",
      "description": "One id held by the root's fallback, by its first child and by both state alternatives of its second child (FUARAN-DUP-ID). Document order puts a node's fallback before its kind and its kind before its state, so the fallback is the first occurrence and the three findings are at $.kind.children[0], $.kind.children[1].state.onEmpty and $.kind.children[1].state.onLoading.",
      "tree": "{\"fallback\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Box\",\"children\":[{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},{\"id\":\"c1\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"},\"state\":{\"onEmpty\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},\"onLoading\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}}}}],\"layout\":{\"$type\":\"Flex\",\"direction\":\"Vertical\"},\"role\":\"Group\"}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "X",
          "path": "$.kind.children[0]"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "X",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1].state.onEmpty"
        },
        {
          "code": "FUARAN-DUP-ID",
          "severity": "Error",
          "node": "X",
          "path": "$.kind.children[1].state.onLoading"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-duplicate-id-across-a-case-the-default-and-the-state",
      "description": "One id held by a Switch's case arm, its default and its own state.onEmpty alternative (FUARAN-DUP-ID): findings at $.kind.default and $.state.onEmpty. The Switch's state key has no writer, so the reference also warns FUARAN103 on it.",
      "tree": "{\"id\":\"root\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Switch\",\"cases\":[{\"child\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},\"match\":\"a\"}],\"default\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}},\"stateKey\":\"k\"},\"state\":{\"onEmpty\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"kind\":{\"$type\":\"Markdown\",\"text\":\"t\"}}}}",
      "expected": [
        {
          "code": "FUARAN103",
          "severity": "Warning",
          "node": "root",
          "path": "$"
